# Which market data the app runs on: yahoo | alphavantage | mock
#
# Leave this unset and you get Yahoo — real prices for real companies, no key, no signup.
# It has no CORS headers, so requests go through the dev-server proxy in vite.config.ts,
# which means it works under `npm run dev` and `npm run preview` but not in a statically
# hosted build with nothing in front of it.
#
# VITE_DATA_SOURCE=yahoo

# Alpha Vantage sends CORS headers, so it works from a static deploy with no proxy. The
# free tier is ~25 requests/day, which a six-position portfolio spends in about four page
# loads even with the cache. Setting a key selects this source unless VITE_DATA_SOURCE
# says otherwise.
#
# Note: VITE_-prefixed variables are inlined into the client bundle at build time. This
# key is visible to anyone who loads a deployed build. Keep it a free-tier key.
#
# VITE_ALPHAVANTAGE_KEY=your_key_here

# `mock` restores the original demo: fictional tickers on a deterministic seeded walk,
# fully offline and repeatable.
#
# VITE_DATA_SOURCE=mock
